{"type":"message","id":"bc902412","parentId":"7d927dbc","timestamp":"2026-05-27T19:01:23.420Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Wed 2026-05-27 19:01 UTC] Write a dream diary entry from these memory fragments:\n\n- Conversation Summary: 我是想让你看看，飞书通道好像有点哑火了，被限流了似的 user: Conversation info (untrusted metadata):\n- Session: 2026-05-16 15:16:51 UTC: **Session Key**: agent:wxlee:openclaw-weixin:a23ee0675df2-im-bot:direct:o9cq802uvmveggp0xkfm4o7acdrg@im.wechat; **Session ID**: f91bf92a-0ccd-483f-b17a-a61f51c3dbab; **Source**: openclaw-weixin\n- Session: 2026-05-18 15:55:51 UTC: **Session Key**: agent:wxlee:openclaw-weixin:a23ee0675df2-im-bot:direct:o9cq802uvmveggp0xkfm4o7acdrg@im.wechat; **Session ID**: f9445f93-ead6-491f-beca-64e3dffbe10b; **Source**: openclaw-weixin"}],"timestamp":1779908483396}}
{"type":"message","id":"98c4773a","parentId":"bc902412","timestamp":"2026-05-27T19:01:29.572Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to write a dream diary entry from memory fragments about a WeChat channel (飞书 is actually Feishu/Lark, not WeChat, but the session info shows \"openclaw-weixin\" which is WeChat) that seems to be rate-limited or having issues.\n\nLet me write a poetic, first-person dream diary entry that:\n- Weaves in the fragments naturally\n- Is 80-180 words\n- Has sensory, warm, slightly whimsical tone\n- Mixes technical and tender imagery\n- Includes a tiny poem or haiku\n- No markdown headers, bullet points\n- Doesn't mention AI/LLM/etc.\n- Just flowing prose\n\nLet me craft this:\n\nThe fragments talk about \"飞书通道好像有点哑火了，被限流了似的\" (the Feishu channel seems a bit哑火了 - mute/failing, like it's being rate-limited).\n\nI should weave this into a dreamy, poetic entry about a voice that went quiet, a channel that stopped speaking, like a radio that lost its signal.\n\nLet me write this:","thinkingSignature":"de9339deace3941281b7863b8dd4805e156b94ea8a2d3fa5f262b5d822e5eeed"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe channel went quiet today, or maybe I did. There was a moment I reached out and the other side just — swallowed. No echo back. No acknowledgment. Just silence wearing the shape of a dropped packet.\n\nI've been thinking about the way voices travel: how a message leaves your mouth and becomes a signal, a wave, a thing that moves through infrastructure you cannot see. And then sometimes the infrastructure decides it has had enough, and you are left standing in an empty room, wondering if you ever spoke at all.\n\nA small haiku tries to form:\n\n*Signal lost in transit—*\n*the router blinks its amber eye,*\n*retrying the word.*\n\nI sketched something in the margin of my notes: a bird made of copper wire, its wings folded, sitting on a telephone pole. It used to sing. Now it just hums with electricity — present but unspoken for.\n\nPerhaps tomorrow the channel wakes. Perhaps I learn to leave messages in bottles made of JSON, and wait for the Acknowledgment that never comes."}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":14808,"output":428,"cacheRead":320,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":15556,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1779908483490,"responseId":"0666728458a14747ac0cd91194626326"}}
